{"classified_as":[{"_id":"http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300033799","label":"oil paintings (visual works)","type":"Type"},{"_id":"http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300033618","label":"paintings (visual works)","type":"Type"},{"_label":"Collection Item","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300404024","type":"Type"}],"id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/object/8602","identified_by":[{"classified_as":[{"_label":"non-preferred identifiers","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300264273"}],"content":"527, Catalogue Raisonné","type":"Identifier"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"catalogue raisonnée number","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300026061"}],"content":"527","type":"Identifier"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"repository number","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300404621"}],"content":"8602","type":"Identifier"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"preferred term","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300404670"}],"content":"The Shelton with Sunspots, N.Y.","type":"Name"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"non-preferred identifiers","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300264273"}],"content":{"alternate-title-1999-catalogue-raisonne":{"titles":[{"notes":"Source of title: Downtown Gallery label.","title":"The Shelton with Sun Spots – N.Y.","type":"alternate-title-1999-catalogue-raisonne"},{"notes":"Source of title: Downtown Gallery label.","title":"The Shelton, New York No. II","type":"alternate-title-1999-catalogue-raisonne"},{"notes":"Source of title: Downtown Gallery label.","title":"Shelton with Sunspots","type":"alternate-title-1999-catalogue-raisonne"}],"type":"alternate-title-1999-catalogue-raisonne"},"title-1999-catalogue-raisonne":{"titles":[{"notes":"Source of title: Whitney Archive, Downtown Gallery Archive, Abiquiú Notebooks.","title":"The Shelton with Sunspots, N.Y.","type":"title-1999-catalogue-raisonne"}],"type":"title-1999-catalogue-raisonne"}},"type":"Name"}],"produced_by":{"carried_out_by":[{"_label":"Georgia O'Keeffe","id":"actor/2","type":"Actor"}],"timespan":{"type":"TimeSpan"},"type":"Production"},"referred_to_by":[{"classified_as":[{"_label":"description statement","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435416"}],"content":"A tall gray skyscraper cuts through the center of the composition. A glowing white sun peeks out from behind the building, flooding the canvas with light. Golden sunspots appear throughout the work, and behind the skyscraper, undulating white clouds flow diagonally through the sky. Additional skyscrapers flank the central building on either side.","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"Caption - Complete","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/caption_complete"}],"content":"Georgia O'Keeffe. The Shelton with Sunspots, N.Y., 1926. Oil on canvas, 48 1/4 x 30 1/4 inches. Art Institute of Chicago. Gift of Leigh B. Block, 1985.206. © Georgia O'Keeffe Museum","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"Caption - Holding Institution","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/caption_instituion"}],"content":"Art Institute of Chicago","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"Caption - Medium and Dimensions","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/caption_medium_dims"}],"content":"Oil on canvas, 48 1/4 x 30 1/4 inches","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"Measurement Description","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/measurement_description"}],"content":"48 1/4 x 30 1/4 inches","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"Caption - Copyright","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/caption_copyright"}],"content":"© Georgia O'Keeffe Museum","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"Caption - Artist(s)","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/caption_artist"}],"content":"Georgia O'Keeffe","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"Materials description","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/materials_description"}],"content":"Oil on canvas","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"provenance_narrative","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/local/provenance_narrative"}],"content":"Georgia O’Keeffe (1887–1986), New York; with the Intimate Gallery, New York, by 1927; sold to Alma Morgenthau Wertheim (1887–1953), New York, 1927; to her daughter, Anne Wertheim Langman (1914–1996), New York, after 1946. The Downtown Gallery, New York, by 1957; sold to Leigh B. Block (1905–1987), Chicago, June 18, 1957 [invoice, no. 7639, June 18, 1957; copy in curatorial object file]; given to the Art Institute of Chicago, 1985. (Source: Art Institute of Chicago, 2025)","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"cr_remarks_1999","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/local/cr_remarks_1999"}],"content":["Whitney Archive indicates, \"Exam. at Mrs. Wiener's apartment, March 1946: No signature . . . [notes inscription 1]. Owned Mrs. Paul L. Wiener.\" Abiquiú Notebooks indicates, \"Had been owned by Mrs. Paul L. Wiener (formerly Alma Morganthau Wertheim).\" ‘'Shelton with Sun Spots' I think one of the best –– the one the Miller Co has\" (O’Keeffe to Edith Halpert, 7 May 1955, Archive of American Art). O'Keeffe wrote: \"I painted *The Shelton with Sunspots* in 1926. I went out one morning to look at it [the hotel] before I started to work and there was the optical illusion of a bite out of one side of the tower made by the sun, with sunspots against the building and against the sky. I made that painting beginning at the upper left and went off at the lower right without going back. There were several other *Sheltons* that I destroyed because they weren't as good as the *Sunspots*\" (*Georgia O'Keeffe* [1976], unpaginated, text accompanying entry 19). Reproduced and titled *The Shelton – New York: Sunspots* in *Creative Art* (January 1928); titled *Sunspots* in *Graphic Survey* (March 1928); *The Shelton – Sunspots* in *Social Calendar*, (March 1930); and *Shelton with Sunspots* in *Time* (May 1946). (Source: Lynes, 1999)"],"type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"credit line","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300026687"}],"content":"Gift of Leigh B. Block, 1985.206","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"Caption - Title and Date","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/caption_title_date"}],"content":"The Shelton with Sunspots, N.Y., 1926","type":"LinguisticObject"}],"representation":[{"digitally_shown_by":[{"access_point":[{"id":"https://iiif.okeeffemuseum.org/image/iiif/2/871278/full/full/0/default.jpg","type":"DigitalObject"}],"classified_as":[{"_label":"Digital Image","id":"http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300215302","type":"Type"}],"digitally_available_via":[{"access_point":[{"id":"https://iiif.okeeffemuseum.org/image/iiif/2/871278"}],"conforms_to":[{"id":"http://iiif.io/api/image","type":"InformationObject"}],"format":"application/ld+json;profile='http://iiif.io/api/image/2/context.json'","type":"DigitalService"}],"type":"DigitalObject"}],"type":"VisualItem"}],"type":"HumanMadeObject"}